This is a patch to add an extended logfile, named "xlogfile", which
is more verbose than the standard logfile.  It's easier to read and to
parse, and also makes it easier to add new fields -- in order to better
accomodate the many ideas for the tournament that require saving
extra information that isn't included in the standard logfile.

Along with it, I've also included code that records:
  The number of turns during the game
  The conduct challenges that were followed
  Whether the player achieved some notable milestones in the game
  The total amount of real time spent playing the game

The first two are things that were recorded during this last tournament;
the last two are things that have come up a few times as being
possibilities for a later tournament.  Any or all of them can be disabled
through definitions in config.h.

Note that this patch does not alter the record / logfile, and so none of
the extra recorded info will be displayed on the top ten lists, unlike
the logmoves patch.

One thing that isn't really finalized is the "notable achievements"
section.  Right now, it keeps track of:

Finishing the quest (either killing the nemesis, or returning the artifact
successfully to your quest leader)

Entering Gehennom (in any way; including level teleporting to the Valley)

Obtaining the Amulet (set when the amulet enters your inventory)

Entering the Elemental Planes

Entering the Astral Plane

Ascending

Comments on other events that might be tracked are welcome.

I'm including the readme here.  The patch is a bit large, so you can
get it from: http://www.u.arizona.edu/~minch/xlog.patch

